<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aror</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Alor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aror, also called Alor, was the capital of medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a>, near modern Rohri and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sukkur">Sukkur</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>. It was the seat of the Rai dynasty and of the Brahman dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tashkent">Chach</a>, and fell to the Arab general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-qasim">Muhammad ibn Qasim</a> in the early 8th century. A shift of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a> away from the city led to its decline, and its ruins lie near the village of Arore.</p></div>
